cat={
'acquisition':('acquisition support','Compare the search criteria, analysis deliverables, inspection support, negotiations, transaction coordination and launch handoff. Identify the person accountable for each stage and the decisions retained by the buyer.','A coordinated search service','A specialist local STR buyer agent','An analyst, agent and launch vendors hired separately','one-time service fees, brokerage costs, independent inspections, design and ongoing management','a signed scope and a sample property decision file'),
'brokerage':('real estate brokerage','Confirm buyer representation, covered markets, commissions, agency duties and transaction support. Separately assign revenue analysis, furnishings, permitting and operating setup if they are outside the brokerage engagement.','A different local STR brokerage','BNB Accelerator acquisition coordination','An independent buyer agent with separately hired analysis support','broker compensation, professional diligence and any separately contracted launch work','the buyer representation agreement and an address-specific due-diligence checklist'),
'turnkey':('turnkey rental investing','Inspect the actual property, intended rental model, construction or rehabilitation status, lease assumptions and the management arrangement. Compare a particular offering with a particular STR purchase rather than treating all turnkey investments as identical.','Another turnkey rental provider','A direct STR purchase with acquisition support','A local agent and independently selected property manager','purchase funding, rehabilitation, service charges, leasing and management costs','a property-specific purchase package and completed-work evidence'),
'fund':('managed investment offerings','Read the offering documents to identify the entity, ownership interest, eligibility, fees, distributions, decision rights and exit constraints. Compare that interest with the capital and responsibilities of direct home ownership.','Another independently reviewed investment offering','Direct property ownership with professional support','A separately evaluated allocation to another asset class','invested capital, offering fees, management fees and any performance allocation','the current offering documents and the full fee waterfall'),
'fractional':('fractional ownership and shared-use models','Identify exactly what is owned, who controls use and rental decisions, who can sell the interest and when. Personal-use co-ownership and an income-oriented investment interest can have materially different objectives.','Another shared-ownership offering','A whole-property purchase','A separately evaluated managed real estate investment','the interest purchase price, shared operating charges, financing and resale costs','the ownership documents, use rules and exit terms'),
'education':('education and coaching','Identify the curriculum, coaching access, actual deal review, enrollment period and refund provisions. Estimate the hours the student must spend sourcing, negotiating, furnishing and operating after the training.','Another curriculum with the skills you need','Self-directed learning plus local specialists','Acquisition coordination when implementation is the immediate need','enrollment, recurring community charges, optional coaching and the capital needed to implement','the enrollment agreement and a written list of live support deliverables'),
'management':('property management and hosting services','Confirm local coverage, listing access, guest support, cleaning oversight, maintenance authority, owner reporting and termination terms. A national brand description cannot substitute for the local agreement covering the address.','Another manager serving the exact address','A local co-host with separately contracted vendors','Owner operation with software and local support','management charges, cleaning, maintenance markups, onboarding and distribution costs','the local management agreement, owner statement and exit procedure'),
'data':('rental data and analysis tools','Test the source, reporting period, comparable property selection and definitions behind revenue and occupancy metrics. Model your own expenses and financing. Data access alone does not assign responsibility for a purchase decision.','Another market-data platform','An independent property analyst','Acquisition support that includes a documented underwriting process','subscriptions, market access, report credits, data exports and separately contracted analysis','a sample report, methodology explanation and the limits of the available dataset'),
'pricing':('revenue management and pricing tools','Compare connected booking channels, minimum and maximum rate controls, rule overrides, occupancy assumptions and the performance reporting period. A recommended nightly rate is a pricing input, not a promise of a reservation.','Another dynamic-pricing platform','A professional revenue manager','A documented owner pricing process with market research','per-listing subscriptions, revenue-based charges, add-ons and integration expenses','the pricing configuration, connected systems and complete billing basis'),
'software':('property-management software','Identify which channels, calendars, payment systems, owner reports and messaging workflows the plan supports. Budget setup and migration, then test a real booking from reservation through payout and owner reporting.','Another compatible property-management system','A smaller software stack for a small portfolio','A local manager using its own disclosed systems','subscription tiers, listing counts, onboarding, payment fees and connected products','the exact product tier, migration plan and a workflow demonstration'),
'marketplace':('marketplaces and distribution platforms','First establish whether the product distributes guest bookings, lists investment property or sells an investment interest. Ask who contracts with the customer, handles money and owns the account and records. A marketplace listing does not complete a property purchase or ongoing operation.','Another platform serving the same transaction','An independently managed direct channel','Specialists hired for the purchase or operating tasks the platform leaves with you','listing charges, transaction fees, commissions, subscriptions and payment processing','the applicable partner or listing terms and a sample transaction reconciliation'),
'operations':('property operations and service tools','Define the problem the product addresses, the hardware or integrations required and who performs the physical work. A notification, task assignment or software workflow only helps when someone is accountable for acting on it.','Another tool for the same operating task','A qualified local service provider','A documented owner process with separately selected tools','hardware, installation, subscriptions, labor, payment charges and replacement costs','the service specification, compatibility list and response responsibilities'),
'insurance':('insurance options','Ask a licensed professional to quote the exact address, property use and ownership structure. Compare insured risks, exclusions, limits, deductibles, business-income definitions and claims obligations using the actual policy documents.','Another appropriately licensed insurance provider','A specialist broker comparing eligible policies','A revised operating plan if suitable coverage is unavailable','premiums, deductibles, endorsements, policy fees and uncovered risk','the written quote, specimen policy and rental-use disclosures')}
notes={
'BNB Mastery':'The reviewed homepage lists BNB Tribe at $49 per month. That is a community price, not a verified price for every coaching program. Ask for the enrollment terms of the specific product you want.',
'STR Search':'The reviewed homepage recommends at least $175,000 for launching an Airbnb venture. That is investment-capital guidance, not an identified service fee. Request a separate acquisition quote.',
'Techvestor':'The reviewed site states a $25,000 minimum investment. A minimum contribution is invested capital, not a complete fee schedule; examine the offering fees and economic allocations separately.',
'Evolve':'The reviewed homepage advertises owner service fees starting at 10%. Confirm the applicable plan, fee base, minimums and excluded local operating costs for your address.',
'Wheelhouse':'The reviewed pricing page lists Pro Flat at $19.99 per listing per month and describes other plan and volume options. Confirm the selected plan and any taxes or additional products.',
'Minut':'The reviewed pricing page lists Starter at $5 per month billed as $60 per year, and Standard at $10 per month per home billed as $120 per year. The sensor is a separate one-time cost. Verify the features and quantity in your order.',
'Turno':'The reviewed pricing page shows a $10 per-property monthly option and a $96 per-property annual option within its plan comparison. Marketplace-cleaner arrangements and non-Turno teammates have different conditions, and cleaning labor is separate. Confirm which conditions apply.',
'HostGPO':'The reviewed pricing page displays a HostGPO membership at $149 per year. Product purchases, delivery and installation remain separate budget items. Confirm the selected membership and current terms.',
'Houst':'The reviewed homepage advertises full-service management from 12%. The current address-specific proposal must identify the fee base, local coverage and all separately charged work.'}
for v in rows:
 name=v['name'];slug=v['slug'];existing=by_slug.get(alias.get(name,'')) or old.get(name.lower())
 if name=='BNB Investor Academy':existing=by_slug.get('michael-elefante')
 if name=='The Real Estate Robinsons':existing=by_slug.get('real-estate-robinsons')
 v['comparisonPath']=existing[4] if existing else '/compare/'+slug+'/'
 oldalt='/compare/alternatives-to-'+(existing[0] if existing else slug)+'/'
 v['alternativesPath']=oldalt
 v['pricingPath']='/compare/'+slug+'-pricing/'
 v['pricingObservation']=notes.get(name,v.get('pricingObservation','A complete current price for your configuration has not been confirmed in this review. Use the official source below to obtain the current plan or written proposal; do not treat a headline price, investment amount or example revenue as the complete service cost.'))
# Choose real, category-relevant peer links from the same researched list.
for v in rows:
 peers=[z for z in rows if z['category']==v['category'] and z['name']!=v['name']]
 v['peerNames']=[z['name'] for z in peers[:3]]

files=[];created=[];blocks={};manifest=[]
def section(q,a):return '<h2>'+E(q)+'</h2><p>'+a+'</p>'
def source(v):
 s=v['source'];pricing=v.get('pricingSource');out='<ul><li><a href="'+E(s['url'],quote=True)+'" target="_blank" rel="noopener">'+E(v.get('displayName',v['name']))+' official website</a></li>'
 if pricing and pricing.get('status')==200:out+='<li><a href="'+E(pricing['url'],quote=True)+'" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official pricing or product page reviewed</a></li>'
 return out+'</ul><p>Primary sources retrieved November 22, 2026. Product names, prices and availability can change. This is BNB Accelerator company-authored buyer guidance; it is not an independent ranking or a customer review.</p>'
def nav(v):return '<nav class="provider-article-nav" aria-label="Related provider guides"><a href="'+v['comparisonPath']+'">Comparison</a><a href="'+v['alternativesPath']+'">Alternatives</a><a href="'+v['pricingPath']+'">Pricing</a><a href="/compare/provider-directory/">All 100 providers</a></nav>'
def faqs(qas):return ''.join(section(q,E(a)) for q,a in qas)
def table(items):return '<div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Option</th><th scope="col">Responsibility to clarify</th></tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join('<tr><th scope="row">'+E(a)+'</th><td>'+E(b)+'</td></tr>' for a,b in items)+'</tbody></table></div>'
for v in rows:
 name=v.get('displayName',v['name']);g=cat[v['category']];label,method,a1,a2,a3,costs,evidence=g;peers=[z for z in rows if z['name'] in v['peerNames']];focus=v['focus'];overview=v['overview'];sourceurl=v.get('pricingSource',v['source'])['url']
 for kind in ['comparison','alternatives','pricing']:
  path=v[kind+'Path'];dest=R/path.strip('/')/'index.html';exists=prior.get(path,dest.exists())
  if kind=='comparison':
   title='BNB Accelerator vs '+name+': scope, cost and buyer FAQ';desc='Compare '+name+' with BNB Accelerator by service scope, owner work, pricing questions and the evidence needed for an STR decision.'
   qas=[('What does '+name+' offer?',overview),('Is '+name+' a direct substitute for BNB Accelerator?','Evaluate the specific contract and your immediate need. This provider is included under '+label+'. BNB Accelerator describes acquisition coordination: sourcing and evaluating property, supporting negotiations and the purchase-to-launch handoff. A tool, education product, booking channel or investment offering can be complementary rather than a replacement.'),('What is the most important '+name+' comparison question?',focus),('How should I compare the actual deliverables?',method),('How should I compare the costs?','Separate '+costs+'. BNB Accelerator service pricing should also come from a current written proposal. Match the same scope, billing period and property count before comparing totals.'),('What evidence should I request before choosing?','Request '+evidence+'. Identify the contracting entity, responsible people, exclusions and exit rights. Review a real example of the work you are purchasing and record what remains your responsibility.')]
   content=faqs(qas)+table([(name,'Confirm the exact '+label+' proposal and the work you retain.'),('BNB Accelerator','Confirm the written acquisition scope, independent vendor costs and buyer approval steps.'),('Independently hired specialists','Name the person coordinating every handoff and deadline.')])+section('Which option fits the next decision?','Start with the work you need completed in the next 30 days. If you need this provider’s specific product, evaluate that product on its own terms. If you need help purchasing a home, compare the documented acquisition responsibilities. Use <a href="/tools/first-str-purchase-budget/">the purchase-budget tool</a> before committing funds.')
  elif kind=='alternatives':
   title=name+' alternatives: scope, pricing and STR buyer FAQ';desc='Explore alternatives to '+name+' by matching the actual STR task, service level, owner workload and full cost.'
   qas=[('Why might I consider alternatives to '+name+'?',overview+' The right reason to compare alternatives is a gap between the offered scope and the work you need completed, rather than a different brand name alone.'),('What should the alternative solve?',focus+' Define the required outcome, expected support, decision rights, implementation time and acceptable contract terms before making a shortlist.'),('Which types of alternatives should I compare?',a1+'; '+a2+'; '+a3+'. These are different routes to completing work, not a claim that every provider offers the same service.'),('Which named providers can I research next?','The related providers below share this guide’s '+label+' category. Their inclusion is a research shortlist, not a ranking or an endorsement of a specific plan. Read their official sources and request current terms.'),('Can BNB Accelerator replace this product?',('BNB Accelerator is an option to evaluate for acquisition coordination. Confirm the exact work in its current proposal and compare it with the alternative contract.' if v['category'] in ['acquisition','brokerage','turnkey'] else 'BNB Accelerator describes property acquisition coordination. It does not automatically replace '+label+'. You may need both acquisition help and a separately selected product or provider for the operating or investment task.')),('How should I choose between the alternatives?',method+' Obtain '+evidence+' from each shortlisted option and compare the same service period and responsibilities.')]
   content=faqs(qas)+'<h2>Related providers in this category</h2><ul>'+''.join('<li><a href="'+z['comparisonPath']+'">'+E(z.get('displayName',z['name']))+'</a>: '+E(z['overview'])+'</li>' for z in peers)+'</ul>'+section('What should I avoid in an alternatives comparison?','Avoid treating a cheaper subscription as a complete substitute for paid execution, or an investment contribution as the same thing as a service fee. Record the work retained by the buyer, the operator and outside professionals. Recheck availability and local coverage for your address.')
  else:
   title=name+' pricing: fees, total cost and buyer FAQ';desc='Review '+name+' pricing questions, the current official source and a practical cost checklist for the specific product or service.'
   qas=[('What does '+name+' cost?',v['pricingObservation']),('What is being priced?',overview+' Confirm the exact product, service tier, property count, billing period, currency, contract term and local availability.'),('Which costs belong in the comparison?','Include '+costs+'. '+focus+' Put recurring charges and one-time implementation costs on separate lines.'),('Is the advertised amount the entire property budget?','No. Distinguish a service charge or subscription from purchase capital and reserves. For a property purchase, separately budget down payment, closing costs, repairs, furnishings, opening costs and retained operating cash. For an operating product, include the labor and connected services needed to use it.'),('What should a written quote show?','Record the contracting entity, selected tier, tax and currency, quantity, due dates, minimum commitment, variable-fee base, cancellation rights, renewal and exclusions. Ask which charges apply when a property is vacant, onboarding is delayed or the service is terminated.'),('How can I compare the annual cost without inventing a vendor price?','Use the actual written quote. Annual service cost equals fixed recurring charges for the year, plus one-time setup, plus variable charges based on your expected usage, plus required third-party costs. Run a lower-usage and a higher-usage case. This is a budgeting method, not a quoted '+name+' fee.')]
   content=faqs(qas)+table([('Fixed recurring charges','Multiply the quoted charge by the stated number of billing periods; verify quantity and currency.'),('Variable charges','Apply the agreed rate to the explicitly defined revenue, transactions, listings or other base.'),('Setup and required extras','Add onboarding, equipment, migration, installation or independent professional costs when applicable.'),('Cancellation and renewal','Document notice, remaining commitments, data access and the price after any promotion ends.')])+section('How should I compare this with BNB Accelerator pricing?','Compare the work delivered. BNB Accelerator publishes acquisition-scope guidance and requests a current written service proposal. Read <a href="/pricing/">BNB Accelerator pricing and scope</a>, then separate any complementary '+E(label)+' expense from the acquisition engagement. Do not replace a service quote with a property example or an income headline.')
  specific=v[{'comparison':'specificComparison','alternatives':'specificAlternatives','pricing':'specificPricing'}[kind]]
  content=section('A '+name+' decision to resolve',E(specific))+content
  body=nav(v)+'<p class="eyebrow">'+E(label.capitalize())+' · reviewed November 22, 2026</p><h1>'+E(title)+'</h1><p class="lead">'+E(overview)+'</p>'+content+'<h2>Official sources and review basis</h2>'+source(v)+nav(v)
  block='<!-- provider-research:start --><section class="section-sm provider-research"><div class="wrap wrap-narrow">'+body+'</div></section><!-- provider-research:end -->'
  if exists:
   s=dest.read_text();s=re.sub(r'<!-- provider-research:start -->.*?<!-- provider-research:end -->','',s,flags=re.S)
   # Existing owner retains its original headline, dates and substantive article.
   block=block.replace('<h1>'+E(title)+'</h1>','<h2>Current '+E(name)+' '+kind+' questions</h2>')
   s=s.replace('</main>',block+'</main>');blocks[path]=block
  else:
   s=tpl.page(title=title+' | BNB Accelerator',description=desc[:160],path=path,body=block,active='/compare/',extra_schema=tpl.article_schema(title,desc[:160],SITE+path,DATE)+tpl.faq_schema(qas));dest.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);created.append(path)
  s=s.replace('</head>','<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/provider-research.css">\n</head>') if '/assets/provider-research.css' not in s else s;dest.write_text(s);files.append(str(dest.relative_to(R)));manifest.append({'provider':v['name'],'category':v['category'],'kind':kind,'path':path,'existingOwner':exists,'source':v['source']['url']})
# One visible directory distinguishes actual acquisition options from adjacent tools and services.
hub='/compare/provider-directory/';groups=collections.defaultdict(list)
for v in rows:groups[v['category']].append(v)
body='<section class="hero hero-page"><div class="wrap wrap-narrow"><p class="eyebrow">100 researched businesses · 300 buyer guides</p><h1>Compare STR acquisition services and related providers</h1><p class="lead">Explore comparison, alternatives and pricing questions for 100 businesses involved in buying, financing, distributing or operating rental property.</p><p>These businesses are grouped by the work they perform. Acquisition teams, courses, managers, investment offerings and software are different choices. The directory does not describe every listed business as a direct substitute for BNB Accelerator.</p><p>Official sources checked November 22, 2026. BNB Accelerator publishes this company-authored directory. Inclusion is not a ranking or a verified customer rating.</p></div></section><section class="section-sm"><div class="wrap wrap-narrow">'
for key,vs in groups.items():
 body+='<h2>'+E(cat[key][0].capitalize())+'</h2><ul>'
 for v in vs:body+='<li><h3>'+E(v.get('displayName',v['name']))+'</h3><p>'+E(v['overview'])+'</p>'+nav(v)+'</li>'
 body+='</ul>'
body+='</div></section>';p=R/hub.strip('/')/'index.html';p.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);p.write_text(tpl.page(title='STR Provider Directory: 100 Comparisons, Alternatives & Pricing',description='Research 100 STR acquisition and related providers by service category, with comparison, alternatives and pricing guides linked to official sources.',path=hub,body=body,active='/compare/'));files.append(str(p.relative_to(R)));created.append(hub)
